## Food swaps

- swap butter and lard for **olive, rapeseed or sunflower oil** and spreads
- choose **lean meat**, and eat more fish, beans and lentils
- have **oily fish**, such as salmon or mackerel, once a week
- eat **oats, barley, nuts and soya**, which can help lower cholesterol
- have fewer cakes, biscuits, pastries and processed meats

## Reading food labels

Look for foods that are **green or amber for saturated fat** on the front of the pack.

## Get moving

Any activity helps. Walking, cycling, swimming and dancing all count.

## Keep up with checks

Have your cholesterol, blood pressure and weight checked as your GP advises. Keep taking your statin unless your GP says otherwise.

## Support

**HEART UK** runs a free cholesterol helpline, and the **British Heart Foundation** has recipes and information.
